{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Over 12 years I’ve built up a stack that I’m genuinely comfortable with,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not just familiar with. Here’s what I use and what I think of each."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"Core-Languages","text":"Core Languages","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Swift","anchor":"Swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"My primary language. I’ve been writing Swift since the early days and have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"watched it mature into one of the best-designed languages in the industry.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Strong opinions on value types, protocol-oriented design, and the right"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use of generics.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Objective-C","anchor":"Objective-C"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Still fluent. Legacy codebases don’t scare me — bridging Swift and ObjC"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in mixed projects is something I’ve done extensively."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"iOS Frameworks","anchor":"iOS-Frameworks"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Framework","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Depth"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"UIKit","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Expert — built complex custom UI, animations, layout systems"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Production experience, follow evolution closely","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"typ